  "routeAdjustment": "Reuse the proved original j-place dichotomy and divisor-support finiteness instead of building restriction to constant fields and fiber finiteness. Reuse native finite simple extensions, finite composita, the infinite Galois correspondence and the discrete-action continuity criterion. The selected external finite-coefficient and finite-orbit separation arguments are adapted directly to existing original function fields, places and Pic0 actions. The two proposition-valued instances are theorem registrations, not construction registrations.",
  "discharged": "Every actual original function over Qbar has a finite field of definition. The original j-place dichotomy and finite normalized-order supports prove that each original place has a finite arithmetic orbit. Functions distinguishing the literal valuation rings yield a finite field fixing the place. A finite compositum over a divisor support fixes its actual degree-zero class. Thus every original Pic0 stabilizer is open in the absolute Galois group. Native open-stabilizer topology proves continuity of the literal arithmetic action on the discrete original torsion, with no finiteness, finite-image or continuity hypothesis supplied.",
  "remaining": "The actual original torsion still requires finiteness and exact cardinality, followed by Tate realization, the rank-two Hecke component and Frobenius/inertia comparison for the normalized cusp eigensystem. Arithmetic automorphy and higher symmetric-power continuation remain open. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20. No acceptance gate closes here.",
